From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:02:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] dt-bindings: display: simple-framebuffer: add
 apple,internal-panel

Add a boolean for a framebuffer that drives the machine's built-in laptop
panel, handed over by the Apple boot loader. simpledrm reports an eDP
connector for such a node instead of an unknown one, so that Omarchy and
other user space do not count the internal panel as an external monitor
and keep holding the lid-switch inhibitor.

The T6050 K114c, K114s, K116c and K116s framebuffer nodes carry it and
failed CHECK_DTBS without it.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>

(cherry picked from commit 67e63a577af4eab860779d28f225247041ae337a)
[k114s: from aurora-silicon/linux pull request 1688 (open draft), unchanged]
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml   | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
index 66e734780..04ed4291d 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
@@ -128,6 +128,14 @@ properties:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description: Display panel node
 
+  apple,internal-panel:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The framebuffer drives the machine's built-in laptop panel, handed over by
+      the boot loader before a display controller driver takes over. simpledrm
+      reports it as an eDP connector instead of an unknown one, so that user
+      space does not count it as an external monitor.
+
   allwinner,pipeline:
     description: Pipeline used by the framebuffer on Allwinner SoCs
     enum:
